<title>BELGIUM: Commission confirms four green rates to devalue on Monday.</title>
<headline>Commission confirms four green rates to devalue on Monday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rates for the mark, guilder, Austrian schilling and Belgian franc will devalue in the European Union's agrimonetary grid on Monday, the European Commission confirmed.</p>
<p>It said the green rate for the mark will devalue to 1.92391 per Ecu, from 1.92047, the Belgian franc to 39.6374 per Ecu, from 39.5483, the Austrian schilling to 13.5355 per Ecu, from 13.5103, and the guilder to 2.15840 per Ecu, from 2.15464.</p>
<p>The UK's Home-Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) earlier forecast the devaluations, caused by the continued strength of the Irish punt which is on course for a possible revaluation.</p>
<p>It also said that sterling will on Monday start a 10-day assessment period for a green rate revaluation.</p>
</text>
